<!--
    kuna `option loopcondhoist` (default-OFF opt-in), S8 goto-quality sub-stage:
    the DEFERRED `ruleBlockIfNoExit` scan inside `CollapseStructure`
    (`p8_structure/blockaction.rs (CollapseStructure::collapse_internal)`).

    The deferred scan walks the live components in order and folds the FIRST one
    whose terminal out-arm qualifies, then restarts the whole rule cascade.  A
    head-tested loop whose exit arm is a `return`  -  after `ActionReturnSplit` /
    `returndup` has given that return in-degree 1  -  is such a component, and it
    sits AHEAD of its own body in that order.  So the head folds to
    `if (!C) return X;`, drops to one out-edge, and `rule_block_while_do` can
    never match it again: the loop is emitted as
    `while( true ) { if (!C) return X; BODY; }`.

    The body block carrying the loop's `break` is a candidate in the SAME scan,
    and folding it first is strictly better  -  the break arm absorbs the loop's
    follower (which the rule's own `size_in() == 1` test already requires be
    reached from nowhere else), the body collapses to a single back-edge clause,
    and the head test hoists into the `while`/`for` header on the next cascade
    pass with no new machinery.  `loopcondhoist on` gives the non-heads one such
    pass and only falls back to the unrestricted upstream pass when it finds
    nothing, so a function with no loop-head candidate is byte-identical.

    Witness (self-contained, 68 bytes at 0x1000, no calls and no relocations):
    `for (; n > 0; n -= 1) if (a[n] == 42) return 1; return 0;` at gcc -O0 x86-64:
    the form-C shape, a head-tested loop whose head exit arm and whose body exit
    arm are two DISTINCT returns.  Same construct as coreutils od read_char and
    libacl getfacl walk_tree_visited in the decbench O0 corpus.

    Pass 1 (default, loopcondhoist off): the bug  -  `while( true ) {` with the
    real loop condition inside it as a guarded exit and the match arm reached by
    `break;`.  Assertions #1 and #3.
    Pass 2 (option loopcondhoist on): the fix  -  the head test is in the header,
    `for (v1 = a1; 0 < v1; v1 = v1 + -1) { if (...) return 1; }`, which is the
    source.  Assertion #2.
-->
